<Layout
	title="About the Journal"
	description="Meet the keeper of Westmarch Fieldnotes, a journal of Middle-earth's roads and quiet corners."
	pubDate={new Date('September 29 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		Westmarch Fieldnotes is a travel journal from a familiar-but-faraway land: one of green hills,
		weathered inns, deep forests, and roads that always seem to lead a little farther than planned.
	</p>

	<h2>Kept by Maeve</h2>
	<p>
		I write down the small things that make a journey feel real: the meal shared after rain, the sound
		of a gate closing at dusk, and the kindness of someone who points out the safer path. These entries
		are for readers who like their adventures with muddy boots and a warm fire at the end.
	</p>

	<p>
		The journal wanders through the Shire, Bree, and beyond, with occasional notes from the scribe's
		desk on maps, language, and the craft of keeping a good record. Make yourself at home; there is
		usually room for one more at the table.
	</p>
</Layout>